      "writtenOn": "2026-11-10T09:02:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done.\n\nNOTE: not as a `/tmp` check. it\u0027s a `tmpfs` on many hosts -\u003e container doesn\u0027t survive a reboot and pointing `NETOPEER_DIR` somewhere persistent is a reason to override it in my opinion; `/tmp` would block that.\n\nINSTEAD: the path is absolute and at least two steps deep, and absent/empty or contain the compose file an earlier run put there. I tested the guard against `/`, `/tmp`, a relative path and `$HOME` -\u003e all refused, including the cases that should pass",
